<title>POLAND: ZLOTY FIXED WEAKER AT 1.16 PCT BELOW PARITY RATE.</title>
<headline>ZLOTY FIXED WEAKER AT 1.16 PCT BELOW PARITY RATE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland on Thursday fixed the zloty at 3.5100 to the dollar, down from 3.5050 on Wednesday and at 1.8695 to the mark, down from 1.8565, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 1.16 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, weaker than Wednesday's fix at -0.94 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
